invalid type: string "HOW A CAR ENGINE WORKS (THE BASICS)\n\nMost cars use an Internal Combustion Engine. This means fuel burns inside the engine to create power. \n\nThe heart of the engine is the CYLINDER. Inside the cylinder is a moving part called a PISTON. The piston moves up and down.\n\nMost car engines use a FOUR-STROKE CYCLE. This happens in four quick steps:", expected f64ÿo,ÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿÿ